{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeFYZ4kgJgLKuZFmSDdju","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014j9eihe8G1ah6jq8h7hkoY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; python3 - <<'PY'\np='DECODE_ZENITH_FINDINGS.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold = '''bug. **Fixing the top-k changes the optimal block size.** Decide block width *after* the kernel fix,\nor you will tune to a transient.\n'''\nnew = '''bug. **Fixing the top-k changes the optimal block size.** Decide block width *after* the kernel fix,\nor you will tune to a transient.\n\n**RESOLVED 2026-08-21 by ladder 2.1, and this caution was right — including about the transient.**\nRe-tuned after 1.1/1.2 over 32 prompts in one load, the optimum moves **6 -> 5**, worth\n**+3.91 +/- 1.65 % tok/s at unchanged `tau` (-0.052 +/- 0.084)**, and everything above 5 is now\nclosed by measurement (7 -1.70 %, 12 -10.86 %, monotone). Note the SIGN: with the verify no longer\nfree the optimum moves DOWN, not up. Priced out of 13,392 verify rounds, one more **drafted**\nposition costs 3.324 +/- 0.281 ms and one more **verified** position 15.184 +/- 0.396 ms, so the\nblock only pays through positions adaptK actually spends — and at BLK=6 the mean realised verify\nwidth was 3.87 of a ceiling of 7. [`wiki/kernel-optimisations.md` §2.13]\n'''\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\n\np='DECODE_LADDER.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold2 = '''      worse than s1, and one of them may already beat the head 2.2 just deployed.**\n      [`measurement-and-traps.md` §22]'''\nnew2 = '''      worse than s1, and one of them may already beat the head 2.2 just deployed.**\n      **Also re-freeze the protocol's block width: it pins `6:1:1.50` in every sweep string, and\n      2.1 moved the served width to 5. Nothing broke silently — the pin is explicit in each script,\n      which is why the default change could not move a frozen protocol under anyone — but a head\n      adjudicated at a width the server no longer uses is being adjudicated off-policy.**\n      [`measurement-and-traps.md` §22]'''\nassert old2 in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old2,new2,1))\nprint('ok')\nPY\necho \"--- verify:\"; grep -n \"RESOLVED 2026-08-21 by ladder 2.1\" DECODE_ZENITH_FINDINGS.md; grep -n \"re-freeze the protocol\" DECODE_LADDER.md","description":"Correct zenith §3.2 and note the protocol pin in 2.4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":156474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d0b6f31-0c0c-4fa3-a8f4-6a7b332bf789","uuid":"82dd0d3d-b17f-43eb-b9ea-4c2ee751907b","timestamp":"2026-08-21T08:03:16.371Z","request_id":"req_011CeFYZ3meFs7w8oe2wuE55"}
