{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeFYbNjU5hNYPVt58jdPm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RaDtE6gJo2VWDovBa4NAfa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_2p1.txt <<'EOF'\n2.1: the speculation block goes 6 -> 5, +3.91 +/- 1.65 % tok/s on 32 prompts AT EQUAL tau -- and making the verify expensive moved the optimum DOWN, not up\n\nWHAT CHANGED. One constant, in the two places that own it: EngineConfig::blk in\ninclude/dsv4_engine.h (the SERVED default -- scripts/serve.sh passes no --blk) and defblk in\nsrc/decode.cu (the bench default). DSV4_BLK=6 still restores the old arm. Every measurement script\nin scripts/ pins its width explicitly in the sweep string, so no frozen protocol moved underneath\nthis; the head-promotion protocol is now off-policy at 6 and that is written into ladder 2.4.\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED. Two palindromic sweeps, each inside ONE checkpoint load, on the live s3\ncheckpoint, adaptK frozen at 1.50, NGEN0 200. Paired per prompt against the shipped BLK=6, bands\n2 SE of the per-prompt differences, n=32:\n\n  BLK=5   +0.926 +/- 0.454 tok/s  = +3.91 +/- 1.65 %   26/32 legs   d tau -0.0518 +/- 0.0835\n  BLK=4   +0.831 +/- 0.576 tok/s  = +3.78 +/- 2.15 %   23/32 legs   d tau -0.2942 +/- 0.1473\n  4 vs 5  -0.095 +/- 0.375 tok/s  = -0.12 +/- 1.43 %                d tau -0.2424 +/- 0.1020\n\n5 is an INTERIOR optimum: 4 buys no throughput over it and does cost acceptance, 6 loses\n3.58 +/- 1.53 %, and the first sweep closes everything above -- 7 -1.70, 8 -2.93, 9 -6.30,\n10 -9.36, 12 -10.86 %, monotone. tau CLIMBS the whole way down, 3.48 -> 4.36, which is why this\nneeded ms/token beside it: a wider block buys the metric the project optimises hardest and charges\nmore than that metric is worth.\n\nWHY. Priced out of the engine's own 13,392 verify rounds (ms_round ~ c0 + cB*BLK + cK*K, fitted per\nprompt, banded across prompts): one more DRAFTED position costs +3.324 +/- 0.281 ms, one more\nVERIFIED position +15.184 +/- 0.396 ms. The draft forward runs at M=BLK whatever adaptK later\ndecides, and adaptK stops early far more often than the ceiling suggests -- at BLK=6 the mean\nrealised verify width is 3.87 of a ceiling of 7 and only 19.3 % of rounds reach it, so 3.13\nproposals per round (10.40 ms) are drafted and thrown away. The sixth proposal buys 0.014 tokens\nper round and costs 5.40 ms. Round-level ms/token: 43.49 (BLK 4) ~ 43.53 (5) << 45.14 (6), computed\nfrom a different field of the same log than the paired result and agreeing with it to a tenth of a\npercent. 5 is also exactly config.json's dspark_block_size -- the width the head was TRAINED at.\nF94 pushed serving one position past training while that position was nearly free; 1.1/1.2 ended\nthat, and DECODE_ZENITH_FINDINGS 3.2 had said in advance that the width would have to be\nre-decided or \"you will tune to a transient\". The transient was 6.\n\nTHE ITEM'S OWN PREDICTION WAS WRONG IN THE DIRECTION IT NAMED, and is corrected rather than quietly\ndropped: it said the optimum \"returns to ~7-9 from an apparent 11-13\". It returns to 5, and the\n\"apparent 11-13\" was never a measurement this repo took -- the default was 6 and F94 had already\nclosed 8. Right mechanism, guessed arithmetic.\n\nWHAT MADE THE FIRST SWEEP UNDER-POWERED WAS NOT REPLICATION. Sweep A gave +2.79 +/- 3.83 % for\nBLK=5 -- the right answer with a band straddling zero -- and more replicates would have bought\nnothing: repeats of the same (prompt, width) emit a BIT-IDENTICAL id sequence (sweep A's own\ndivergence table shows every first-divergence index twice, once per mirror), so a repeat cancels\ntiming drift and nothing else, and sweep B measured that drift at +0.000 +/- 0.002 tok/s over 99\nmirrored pairs. The band was between-PROMPT variance; the only estimator that shrinks it is more\nprompts. n 8 -> 32 took the band 3.83 -> 1.65 % with the point estimate essentially unmoved. Subsets\nagree: suite-8 +2.70 +/- 3.82 %, the 24 held-out prompts +4.32 +/- 1.82 %.\n\nGATES. Not bit-exact by construction (BLK sets M in the verify forward, hence MoE atomic reduction\norder), so this ships under invariant 1's second branch: LOSSLESS gate 24/24 points PASS across both\nsweeps, and DSV4_GENOUT recorded all 344 emitted sequences -- divergence from the BLK=6 reference is\nalways LATE (first difference at token 213-284) and identical on both mirrors. The served default\nwas proven behaviourally, not by reading source: \"[engine] loading .../ckpt-head-s3 (seqmax=8192,\nblk=5, adaptK=1.50)\" from a real run_server.sh load (detached, ppid systemd, tty ?), and\n\"[parse] point 0: BLK=5\" from build/decode with no DSV4_BLK. The four cheap server gates\n(tokenizer/encoding/api/stream) pass on the rebuilt binary. No re-measurement was needed after the\nrebuild: both arms were measured by the SAME binary in the same load.\n\nEvidence: evidence/decode_loop/{blkwidth_verdict_c32.txt, blkwidth_sweep_c32.log,\nblkwidth_genout_c32.txt, blkwidth_c32.log, 2p1_server_proof.log} + iteration 11's blkwidth_*.\nCorpus: protocol/blkwidth_corpus.txt (8 frozen suite prompts + 24 s3 hold-out prompts truncated to\n192 ids). Wiki: kernel-optimisations.md 2.13, negative-results.md 4k, measurement-and-traps.md 37,\nREADME state table; DECODE_ZENITH_FINDINGS.md 3.2 resolved.\nEOF\nwc -l evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_2p1.txt; head -1 evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_2p1.txt | wc -c","description":"Write the prepared commit message"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2278,"cache_read_input_tokens":158957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2278},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_