{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeFYnBfm9PciadLFuKQzP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ENiZ79ekE4fnfjbFDqfmgZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; python3 - <<'PY'\np='DECODE_LADDER.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold = '''      **NOT BIT-EXACT BY CONSTRUCTION, PRE-REGISTERED AS SUCH, AND MEASURED.** BLK sets M in the\n      verify forward and therefore MoE atomic reduction order, so this ships under invariant 1's\n      SECOND branch. The LOSSLESS gate (first 8 tokens vs base AR) PASSES at every width in both\n      sweeps, 24/24 points, and `DSV4_GENOUT` recorded all 199 + 145 emitted sequences: at BLK=5 the\n      text diverges from the BLK=6 reference on most prompts, always **late** (first divergence at\n      token 213-284 of 200 generated + prompt), never early, and identically on both mirrors.'''\nnew = '''      **PRE-REGISTERED AS NOT BIT-EXACT, AND THEN MEASURED AS BIT-EXACT -- 258 comparisons, ZERO\n      differing tokens.** BLK sets M in the verify forward and therefore MoE atomic reduction order,\n      so the sweep was written to ship under invariant 1's SECOND branch and to *measure* the\n      divergence rather than assume it. It measures none. The LOSSLESS gate (first 8 tokens vs base\n      AR) PASSES at every width in both sweeps, 24/24 points; and across all 344 sequences\n      `DSV4_GENOUT` recorded, **every non-reference arm is id-for-id identical to the BLK=6\n      reference over every position the two have in common** -- 126 comparisons at widths 4-12 in\n      sweep A, 132 at widths 4-5 in sweep B, **0 genuinely differing tokens in either**.\n\n      **The first reading of that table said otherwise, and the defect was in the reader.**\n      `blkwidth_ab.py` counted a length difference as a divergence and printed a \"first divergence\"\n      index that was really the end of the shorter sequence -- so 70 of 132 sweep-B arms read as\n      divergent when their ids are equal. Generation stops at the first verify that carries the\n      count past NGEN, so a narrower block overshoots 200 by a different amount and the sequences\n      simply END at different positions (-6 to +7 tokens). That is bit-exactness up to the stop\n      rule. It is [`measurement-and-traps.md` §35](wiki/measurement-and-traps.md) inverted: §35 read\n      a byte-identity gate PAST the length where the arms agree and called a real difference a pass;\n      this read one past that length and called an agreement a failure. Both verdict files were\n      regenerated with the fixed classifier, which now reports the three cases separately.\n\n      So the emitted text does not depend on the block width at all on this corpus, and the MoE\n      atomic-order risk the pre-registration named did not produce a single differing token.'''\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nprint('ok')\nPY\ngrep -n \"258 comparisons\" DECODE_LADDER.md","description":"Correct the bit-exactness claim in the ladder"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":175846,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1320},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d0b6f31-0c0c-4fa3-a8f4-6a7b332bf789","uuid":"7e9df2c3-90e6-4131-b699-c3633917ef80","timestamp":"2026-08-21T08:06:16.446Z","request_id":"req_011CeFYnA8kBJwVzKYq4yw6J"}
