{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeFYvMnCXaxSZpTtdfgvL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration 12 done — ladder item **2.1** completed, one kernel-adjacent change shipped.\n\n## The change\n\n`EngineConfig::blk` and `src/decode.cu`'s `defblk`: **6 → 5**. `serve.sh` passes no `--blk`, so the header default *is* the served width. Proven behaviourally, not by reading source: `[engine] loading .../ckpt-head-s3 (seqmax=8192, blk=5, adaptK=1.50)` from a real detached `run_server.sh` load, and `[parse] point 0: BLK=5` from `build/decode`. `DSV4_BLK=6` restores the old arm.\n\n## The measurement\n\nIteration 11 had run a 9-prompt sweep and stopped without deciding — its BLK=5 result was **+2.79 ± 3.83 %**, right answer, band straddling zero. More replicates would have bought nothing: repeats of a (prompt, width) cell are id-identical (173 mirrored pairs, 173 identical, 0 differing), so a repeat cancels timing drift only. The band was between-*prompt* variance, so I widened the corpus to 32 prompts (8 frozen suite + 24 `s3` hold-out prefixes) and re-ran in one load, palindromic, adaptK frozen:\n\n| BLK vs 6, n=32 | d % tok/s | legs + | d tau |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **5** | **+3.91 ± 1.65 %** | 26/32 | −0.052 ± 0.084 (covers zero) |\n| 4 | +3.78 ± 2.15 % | 23/32 | −0.294 ± 0.147 |\n| 4 vs 5 | −0.12 ± 1.43 % | 15/32 | −0.242 ± 0.102 |\n\n5 is an interior optimum — 4 buys no throughput and costs acceptance; sweep A closes 7…12 (−1.70 to −10.86 %, monotone). Within-load drift measured at +0.000 ± 0.002 tok/s.\n\n**Mechanism**, out of 13,392 verify rounds: a drafted position costs 3.324 ± 0.281 ms, a *verified* one 15.184 ± 0.396. At BLK=6 the mean realised verify width is 3.87 of a ceiling of 7 — the sixth proposal buys 0.014 tokens/round and costs 5.40 ms. Round-level ms/token (43.49 / 43.53 / 45.14 for 4/5/6) reproduces the paired result from a different field of the same log. 5 is also exactly `config.json`'s `dspark_block_size`: F94's 6 was correct for an engine where `k_topk_verify<<<K,32>>>` ran one active thread, and 1.1/1.2 ended that.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n- **The item's own prediction was wrong in the direction it named** (\"optimum returns to ~7-9\"); the expensive verify moves it *down*, and the \"apparent 11-13\" was never measured here.\n- **It's bit-exact, though pre-registered not to be.** My first pass reported divergences; the analyser was counting a different *length* as a different token. Corrected: 258 arm-vs-reference comparisons at widths 4–12, **zero differing tokens** — the arms only stop at different points (−6 to +7 past NGEN). Fixed the classifier, regenerated both verdicts, and wrote it up as §35's trap run backwards.\n\nWiki: `kernel-optimisations.md` §2.13, `negative-results.md` §4k, `measurement-and-traps.md` §37, README state table, `DECODE_ZENITH_FINDINGS.md` §3.2 resolved. Ladder 2.4 and P2.6 updated (P2.6's headroom drops to +1.85 % oracle over static 5). Commit message prepared at `evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_2p1.txt` for the loop driver — I don't hold git permissions.\n\nOne thing you should know: `scripts/stop_after_2p1.sh`, a watcher left by an earlier iteration, saw `- [x] **2.1` and touched `DECODE_LOOP_STOP` at 04:01. The loop will stop cleanly at the next top-of-loop rather than continue to 2.3. I left that in place — it was a deliberate prior decision, not something for me to overturn."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1033,"cache_read_input_tokens":190267,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1033},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d0b6f31-0c0c-4fa3-a8f4-6a7b332bf789","uuid":"7fafcd71-5170-4f18-ba47-d16c7cbbac4f","timestamp":"2026-08-21T08:08:12.182Z","request_id":"req_011CeFYvLLPJB4BNSB8A4HWM"}
